# Device patch paths, one per line in application order.
#
# Two core patches are named by neither the ARM64 nor the OS series, and the
# official records say they must still be present:
# docs/xnu/patch-reference.md lists native-smp-secondary under "Platform and
# CPU", and docs/.vitepress/device-records/sirius.toml records for sdm710 that
# "the ARM64 and OS series assume the two files they omit are present ... Both
# now live in the sdm710 SoC series, which applies before the OS series".
# UniXNU-sm8250-common@6bb9b025 ships an empty patches/xnu/series, so the board
# layer supplies them here, referencing the core-owned files through the same
# arch: prefix the OS series uses for zzz-boot-progress.patch; nothing here is
# a device-local rewrite of XNU.
#
# native-smp-secondary: MAX_CPUS 4 -> 8 plus MPIDR Affinity1 core numbering for
# BCM2837. dts/sm8250.dtsi numbers this board's eight Kryo 585 cores as
# reg = <0 0x0 0x100 ... 0x700>, i.e. the core index sits in Affinity1, so
# without this patch sheng-smp=1 still brings up one core.
#
# sheng-platform-power: the sheng_pmgr_run() call site in bsd_init.c that
# CONFIG_XNU_SHENG_PMGR=y needs, and the block zzz-boot-progress.patch quotes as
# unchanged context at its @@ -773,7 +775,9 @@ hunk.
#
# Order in [kernel] patch_series: this file is listed before os: rather than
# last. git apply runs the resolved sequence literally (scripts/unixnu/patches.py
# prepare), and the OS series' zzz-boot-progress.patch hunk only applies once the
# block above already exists, so the canonical arch/soc/os/device order cannot be
# satisfied while the SoC series stays empty.
arch:../../../patches/xnu/native-smp-secondary.patch
arch:../../../patches/xnu/sheng-platform-power.patch
